fix(admin): the feedback banner said "needs attention" on a healthy channel

StateBanner accepts "on" | "off" | "danger". The feedback card passed "ok", which matches none
of them, so the component's ternary fell through to the warning colour: an enabled, fully wired
channel rendered in amber, next to cards that genuinely were broken. It did not crash and
nothing was logged - the toggle beside it was correctly blue and the webhook URL was shown, so
only the banner was lying.

The same commit makes the class impossible to ship again. admin had no typecheck anywhere: its CI
ran vitest and vite build, and esbuild strips types without checking them, so TS2322 on this exact
line was invisible. "npm run typecheck" now exists in admin and runs in the CI job ahead of the
tests, matching what mobile already does. Running it against main first showed this was the only
error, so enabling it costs nothing today.

The tone decision moves into an exported pure function so it is assertable at all - a colour
computed inline inside a card is not something a test can reach. The four cases: on, off,
not-configured outranking the toggle in both directions, and a sweep asserting that only tones
StateBanner accepts are ever returned.